    "result_text": "All 32 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement (checkpoint **Cp21**, `audit-create`) in the owner create flow.\n\n**Change:** `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n\n1. Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. Emit an audit line immediately after a successful save in `addOwner(...)`, carrying the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate:\n   ```java\n   this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line is logged only on the success path (after all validation/rejection rules pass and the owner is persisted), and the `customerCode`/`registrationDate` values are the finalized, stored ones \u2014 matching what the test reads back via `GET`. The test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches a Logback appender to the `AUDIT` logger and confirms a single line contains all three values. The full suite (32 tests) is green.",
